          "title": "Two Pointers and Prefix Sums",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Pointers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Opposite ends: `l=0`, `r=n-1` on a ==sorted== array",
                "Sum too small → `l += 1`; too large → `r -= 1`",
                "{green:O(n)} time, {green:O(1)} space",
                "Slow/fast: ==slow== writes, ==fast== reads (in-place dedupe, remove-element)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Prefix Sums",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pre[i+1] = pre[i] + a[i]`, so `pre` has length ==n+1==",
                "`sum(l..r) = pre[r+1] - pre[l]`: O(1) after O(n) build",
                "Subarray sum = k: map of prefix sum → count",
                "Each step add `cnt[run - k]`, then count `run`; O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def count_k(a, k):",
                "    cnt, run, res = {0: 1}, 0, 0",
                "    for x in a:",
                "        run += x",
                "        res += cnt.get(run - k, 0)",
                "        cnt[run] = cnt.get(run, 0) + 1",
                "    return res"
              ],
              "note": "seed {0: 1} so prefixes starting at index 0 count"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choose by Problem",
